        "Thin with water, a teaspoon at a time, if it is stiffer than spreadable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "assembly",
      "tree": {
        "op": "frost",
        "detail": "thin crumb coat,\nchill 20 min,\nthen frost fully",
        "children": [
          {
            "op": "chill",
            "detail": "uncovered,\n30 min – 2 hr",
            "children": [
              {
                "op": "stack",
                "detail": "center and\npress gently",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "item": "cooled cake layers",
                    "from": "cake"
                  },
                  {
                    "item": "about 1 cup frosting",
                    "from": "frosting"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "item": "remaining frosting",
            "from": "frosting"
          }
        ]
      },
      "prep": [
        "Set the first layer on the plate with parchment strips under the edges"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    {
      "title": "Weigh the flour",
      "body": "Or spoon it into the cup and sweep the excess off — scooping straight from the bag packs in far too much."
    },
    {
      "title": "Hot milk, not warm",
      "body": "Bring the milk to a simmer before the butter and oil go in, so everything melts and the batter stays smooth when it is added."
    },
    {
      "title": "Doneness",
      "body": "Edges pull away, a toothpick comes out clean, and the centre reads 205°F. Cool 15 minutes in the pans before turning out."
    },
    {
      "title": "Chill between coats",
      "body": "Half an hour in the fridge after stacking, then a thin crumb coat and 20 minutes more, makes the final coat far easier to smooth."
    },
    {
      "title": "Keeping",
      "body": "Covered at room temperature up to 3 days, refrigerated up to a week, or frozen up to a month."
    }
  ]
}
